(window.XZ_MANUAL_CHAPTERS=window.XZ_MANUAL_CHAPTERS||{})["mods-menu"]="<header class=\"mc-head\"><p class=\"mc-eyebrow\">MODS menu<\/p><h2 class=\"mc-title\" tabindex=\"-1\">The MODS menu<\/h2><p class=\"mc-lede\">How to open MODS, move around it with the encoder or touch, and what is on every section page.<\/p><p class=\"applies\" data-applies=\"both\">Applies to <b>MODERN and CLASSIC<\/b><\/p><\/header><p>MODS is the menu XZ Mods adds to the player. Everything the mod can change lives here, sorted by what you want to do rather than by how the firmware is built. Both interfaces open the same menu, so what you learn here works in MODERN and CLASSIC. MODERN draws it in the FLAGSHIP look. CLASSIC draws it in the theme you chose.<\/p>\n<h3 id=\"m-open-and-close-mods\" data-anchor=\"open-and-close-mods\">Open and close MODS<\/h3>\n<p>Press <kbd>MENU<\/kbd> on the play screen. A short press opens MODS wherever the player's own firmware has no job for <kbd>MENU<\/kbd>, and leaves the stock job alone everywhere else. Hold <kbd>MENU<\/kbd> to open the player's own UTILITY, exactly as on a stock XDJ-XZ.<\/p>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Where you are<\/th><th>Short press of <kbd>MENU<\/kbd><\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>The MODS menu is open<\/td><td>Closes MODS<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>A game is on screen<\/td><td>The game's own key<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>The VJ.Tools view is on screen<\/td><td>As before<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>A menu, popup or dialog is open<\/td><td>Works or closes the open menu<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>A track list (browse, playlist, search, history)<\/td><td>The sort menu or the track menu<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>TAG LIST<\/td><td>LIST MENU<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>The play screen in GRID ADJUST<\/td><td>The beat grid menu<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>The play screen<\/td><td>Opens MODS <span class=\"tag tag--experimental\">experimental<\/span><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>The SOURCE screen<\/td><td>Opens MODS <span class=\"tag tag--experimental\">experimental<\/span><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>The track INFO screen<\/td><td>Opens MODS <span class=\"tag tag--experimental\">experimental<\/span><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>The SHORTCUT screen<\/td><td>Opens MODS <span class=\"tag tag--experimental\">experimental<\/span><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>The player's own UTILITY<\/td><td>Closes UTILITY<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Any other screen<\/td><td>The screen's own job<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div>\n<aside class=\"callout callout--note\"><b>Note<\/b><p>Rows marked experimental follow the XDJ-XZ operating instructions but have not been checked on every firmware version yet. If a press does something different on your player, <span class=\"m-ext\">report it <span class=\"m-url\">github.com/OpticMystic/XZ-Mods/issues<\/span><\/span>.<\/p><\/aside>\n<p>To leave MODS, press <kbd>MENU<\/kbd> again, tap <strong>CLOSE<\/strong> in the top right corner, or press <kbd>BACK<\/kbd> until you are back on the play screen.<\/p>\n<p>You can also open MODS from the <strong>MODS<\/strong> button at the top of the MODERN play screen, or from the button next to LINK when you set it to <strong>MODS MENU<\/strong> in <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"mods-menu\" data-anchor=\"play\">PLAY<\/a>.<\/p>\n<h3 id=\"m-move-around\" data-anchor=\"move-around\">Move around<\/h3>\n<p>You can drive the whole menu with the rotary encoder, with touch, or with both.<\/p>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Control<\/th><th>What it does in MODS<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>Turn the encoder<\/td><td>Moves the highlight to the next card, row or button<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Push the encoder<\/td><td>Opens or changes the highlighted item<\/td><\/tr><tr><td><kbd>BACK<\/kbd><\/td><td>Goes up one level: from an open item to its page, then from a page to the section rail<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Tap<\/td><td>Opens or changes whatever you tap<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div>\n<p>The hints in the bottom right corner (<strong>TURN MOVE · PUSH SELECT · BACK UP<\/strong>) always show what the encoder and <kbd>BACK<\/kbd> will do next.<\/p>\n<p>Every page has the same frame. The section rail on the left lists HOME, PLAY, STEMS, SCREEN, 4 DECKS, CONNECT and EXTRAS. The dock along the bottom explains whatever is highlighted. On the right of the dock, <strong>WORKS ON<\/strong> shows which decks the highlighted feature works on, in mixer order 3 1 2 4. A dimmed number means the feature does not work on that deck, and a short amber line says why.<\/p>\n<h3 id=\"m-home\" data-anchor=\"home\">HOME<\/h3>\n<p>HOME is the first page. It shows one card for each section, with a one-line summary of what the section does and the current state of its most important setting, so you can see at a glance whether stems are ready or four decks are connected.<\/p>\n<figure class=\"mf\" id=\"f-mods-menu-1\"><div class=\"mf-frame\"><div class=\"mf-bar\"><span class=\"mf-label\">MODS · HOME<\/span><\/div><div class=\"mf-stage\"><img src=\"manual/shots/56d7ed30848a0120.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"The HOME page with stems ready and four decks not connected yet.\" data-iface=\"modern\"><img src=\"manual/shots/6953688aa006c458.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"The HOME page with stems ready and four decks not connected yet.\" data-iface=\"classic\"><span class=\"mf-spot\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span><div class=\"mf-marks\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Numbered points on the picture\"><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"1\" data-x=\"11.875\" data-y=\"4.167\" aria-label=\"1: BACK\" aria-describedby=\"f-mods-menu-1-1\">1<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"2\" data-x=\"13.125\" data-y=\"62.500\" aria-label=\"2: Section rail\" aria-describedby=\"f-mods-menu-1-2\">2<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"3\" data-x=\"28.125\" data-y=\"13.958\" aria-label=\"3: Section card\" aria-describedby=\"f-mods-menu-1-3\">3<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"4\" data-x=\"68.750\" data-y=\"41.042\" aria-label=\"4: Status line\" aria-describedby=\"f-mods-menu-1-4\">4<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"5\" data-x=\"31.250\" data-y=\"69.792\" aria-label=\"5: Setup button\" aria-describedby=\"f-mods-menu-1-5\">5<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"6\" data-x=\"15.625\" data-y=\"88.542\" aria-label=\"6: Dock\" aria-describedby=\"f-mods-menu-1-6\">6<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"7\" data-x=\"89.000\" data-y=\"88.542\" aria-label=\"7: Save state\" aria-describedby=\"f-mods-menu-1-7\">7<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"8\" data-x=\"95.000\" data-y=\"92.708\" aria-label=\"8: Encoder hints\" aria-describedby=\"f-mods-menu-1-8\">8<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"9\" data-x=\"97.000\" data-y=\"9.583\" aria-label=\"9: CLOSE\" aria-describedby=\"f-mods-menu-1-9\">9<\/button><\/div><\/div><\/div><figcaption>The HOME page with stems ready and four decks not connected yet.<\/figcaption><ol class=\"mf-legend\" aria-label=\"What the numbers show\"><li data-n=\"1\" id=\"f-mods-menu-1-1\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1<\/span><div><b>BACK<\/b> <span>Goes up one level. On HOME it closes MODS.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"2\" id=\"f-mods-menu-1-2\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2<\/span><div><b>Section rail<\/b> <span>Every section of MODS, top to bottom. Tap one, or turn the encoder while the rail is highlighted.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"3\" id=\"f-mods-menu-1-3\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3<\/span><div><b>Section card<\/b> <span>Opens that section. The highlighted card has a light outline.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"4\" id=\"f-mods-menu-1-4\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">4<\/span><div><b>Status line<\/b> <span>The state of the section's main setting. Green means ready, amber means it needs you.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"5\" id=\"f-mods-menu-1-5\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">5<\/span><div><b>Setup button<\/b> <span>Appears when a feature needs setting up, and starts a short guide for it.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"6\" id=\"f-mods-menu-1-6\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">6<\/span><div><b>Dock<\/b> <span>Explains the highlighted item in plain words before you open it.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"7\" id=\"f-mods-menu-1-7\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">7<\/span><div><b>Save state<\/b> <span>Confirms your changes are saved to the USB, or says why they cannot be.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"8\" id=\"f-mods-menu-1-8\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">8<\/span><div><b>Encoder hints<\/b> <span>What turning, pushing and BACK will do right now.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"9\" id=\"f-mods-menu-1-9\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">9<\/span><div><b>CLOSE<\/b> <span>Closes MODS and returns to where you were.<\/span><\/div><\/li><\/ol><\/figure>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Card<\/th><th>Its status line shows<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>PLAY<\/td><td>Your beat jump sizes, page 1 then page 2<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>STEMS<\/td><td>Not set up, Off, or On with the state of deck 1 and deck 2<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>SCREEN<\/td><td>The interface, the waveform colours and the key notation<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>4 DECKS<\/td><td>Not connected, Looking for the cable, Starting decks 3 and 4, Ready with the deck view, Could not start, Disconnected, or Not available on this player<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>CONNECT<\/td><td>Your DJ profile and its USB, and whether VJ.Tools is connected<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>EXTRAS<\/td><td>The games and how many USB apps are on the stick<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div>\n<p>Two setup buttons can appear on HOME. <strong>SET UP USB STEMS<\/strong> opens the USB stems guide when the stem engine is not ready. <strong>SET UP FOUR DECKS<\/strong> opens 4 DECKS when no cable is found, a start failed, the cable was lost, or the USB loader has no four-deck engine.<\/p>\n<h3 id=\"m-play\" data-anchor=\"play\">PLAY<\/h3>\n<p>PLAY changes what the pads and buttons do while you perform.<\/p>\n<figure class=\"mf\" id=\"f-mods-menu-2\"><div class=\"mf-frame\"><div class=\"mf-bar\"><span class=\"mf-label\">MODS · PLAY<\/span><\/div><div class=\"mf-stage\"><img src=\"manual/shots/7d55955e4fefd8fe.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"MODS · PLAY\" data-iface=\"modern\"><img src=\"manual/shots/a622ef27fd10f75d.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"MODS · PLAY\" data-iface=\"classic\"><span class=\"mf-spot\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span><div class=\"mf-marks\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Numbered points on the picture\"><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"1\" data-x=\"16.000\" data-y=\"17.500\" aria-label=\"1: BEAT JUMP PADS\" aria-describedby=\"f-mods-menu-2-1\">1<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"2\" data-x=\"16.000\" data-y=\"27.500\" aria-label=\"2: GATE CUE and SMART CUE\" aria-describedby=\"f-mods-menu-2-2\">2<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"3\" data-x=\"57.750\" data-y=\"40.833\" aria-label=\"3: KEYS and RAM TRACKS\" aria-describedby=\"f-mods-menu-2-3\">3<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"4\" data-x=\"16.000\" data-y=\"54.167\" aria-label=\"4: BUTTON NEXT TO LINK\" aria-describedby=\"f-mods-menu-2-4\">4<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"5\" data-x=\"90.250\" data-y=\"88.542\" aria-label=\"5: WORKS ON\" aria-describedby=\"f-mods-menu-2-5\">5<\/button><\/div><\/div><\/div><ol class=\"mf-legend\" aria-label=\"What the numbers show\"><li data-n=\"1\" id=\"f-mods-menu-2-1\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1<\/span><div><b>BEAT JUMP PADS<\/b> <span>Your own beat jump distances for both pad pages. The row shows the sizes now in use.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"2\" id=\"f-mods-menu-2-2\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2<\/span><div><b>GATE CUE and SMART CUE<\/b> <span>Switch each cue trick on or off. A feature the player has not reported yet shows a SET UP button instead.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"3\" id=\"f-mods-menu-2-3\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3<\/span><div><b>KEYS and RAM TRACKS<\/b> <span>Open their own pages.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"4\" id=\"f-mods-menu-2-4\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">4<\/span><div><b>BUTTON NEXT TO LINK<\/b> <span>What the media button next to LINK does on a press, and with SHIFT.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"5\" id=\"f-mods-menu-2-5\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">5<\/span><div><b>WORKS ON<\/b> <span>The decks the highlighted feature works on.<\/span><\/div><\/li><\/ol><\/figure>\n<p><a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"performance\">Beat jump and performance features<\/a> explains every item on this page.<\/p>\n<h3 id=\"m-stems\" data-anchor=\"stems\">STEMS<\/h3>\n<p>STEMS mutes vocals, harmonics and drums from the pads or the screen.<\/p>\n<figure class=\"mf\" id=\"f-mods-menu-3\"><div class=\"mf-frame\"><div class=\"mf-bar\"><span class=\"mf-label\">MODS · STEMS<\/span><\/div><div class=\"mf-stage\"><img src=\"manual/shots/28154eae613bce65.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"MODS · STEMS\" data-iface=\"modern\"><img src=\"manual/shots/bb2c98f94c514237.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"MODS · STEMS\" data-iface=\"classic\"><span class=\"mf-spot\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span><div class=\"mf-marks\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Numbered points on the picture\"><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"1\" data-x=\"16.000\" data-y=\"17.500\" aria-label=\"1: USB STEMS\" aria-describedby=\"f-mods-menu-3-1\">1<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"2\" data-x=\"16.000\" data-y=\"30.833\" aria-label=\"2: STEM PADS\" aria-describedby=\"f-mods-menu-3-2\">2<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"3\" data-x=\"16.000\" data-y=\"48.958\" aria-label=\"3: Stem buttons on screen\" aria-describedby=\"f-mods-menu-3-3\">3<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"4\" data-x=\"16.000\" data-y=\"65.833\" aria-label=\"4: STEM COLOURS\" aria-describedby=\"f-mods-menu-3-4\">4<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"5\" data-x=\"90.250\" data-y=\"88.542\" aria-label=\"5: WORKS ON\" aria-describedby=\"f-mods-menu-3-5\">5<\/button><\/div><\/div><\/div><ol class=\"mf-legend\" aria-label=\"What the numbers show\"><li data-n=\"1\" id=\"f-mods-menu-3-1\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1<\/span><div><b>USB STEMS<\/b> <span>Switches stems from the USB on or off. Reads SET UP USB STEMS until the stem engine is ready.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"2\" id=\"f-mods-menu-3-2\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2<\/span><div><b>STEM PADS<\/b> <span>Which pad mode and pad bank the stems use.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"3\" id=\"f-mods-menu-3-3\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3<\/span><div><b>Stem buttons on screen<\/b> <span>Where the stem buttons sit on the play screen. Each picture is one layout.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"4\" id=\"f-mods-menu-3-4\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">4<\/span><div><b>STEM COLOURS<\/b> <span>The colours of drums, harmonics and vocals.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"5\" id=\"f-mods-menu-3-5\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">5<\/span><div><b>WORKS ON<\/b> <span>Only decks 1 and 2 are lit. The amber line under it says decks 3 and 4 have no stems.<\/span><\/div><\/li><\/ol><\/figure>\n<p>STEMS IN DJ SOFTWARE sets up stems for a computer playing through the player. MODERN adds a <strong>BYPASS BUTTON<\/strong> switch beside STEM COLOURS. <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"stems\">Stems<\/a> explains every item on this page.<\/p>\n<h3 id=\"m-screen\" data-anchor=\"screen\">SCREEN<\/h3>\n<p>SCREEN sets how the play screen looks.<\/p>\n<figure class=\"mf\" id=\"f-mods-menu-4\"><div class=\"mf-frame\"><div class=\"mf-bar\"><span class=\"mf-label\">MODS · SCREEN<\/span><\/div><div class=\"mf-stage\"><img src=\"manual/shots/cb5c523ef44bb366.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"MODS · SCREEN\" data-iface=\"modern\"><img src=\"manual/shots/95a1b2af251c609a.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"MODS · SCREEN\" data-iface=\"classic\"><span class=\"mf-spot\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span><div class=\"mf-marks\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Numbered points on the picture\"><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"1\" data-x=\"16.000\" data-y=\"20.833\" aria-label=\"1: INTERFACE\" aria-describedby=\"f-mods-menu-4-1\">1<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"2\" data-x=\"66.250\" data-y=\"11.250\" aria-label=\"2: DECK VIEW\" aria-describedby=\"f-mods-menu-4-2\">2<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"3\" data-x=\"16.000\" data-y=\"34.167\" aria-label=\"3: THEME\" aria-describedby=\"f-mods-menu-4-3\">3<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"4\" data-x=\"85.000\" data-y=\"34.167\" aria-label=\"4: 3-BAND COLOURS\" aria-describedby=\"f-mods-menu-4-4\">4<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"5\" data-x=\"16.000\" data-y=\"47.500\" aria-label=\"5: WAVEFORM COLOURS\" aria-describedby=\"f-mods-menu-4-5\">5<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"6\" data-x=\"98.750\" data-y=\"41.250\" aria-label=\"6: KEY NOTATION\" aria-describedby=\"f-mods-menu-4-6\">6<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"7\" data-x=\"16.000\" data-y=\"60.833\" aria-label=\"7: Keys and the track list\" aria-describedby=\"f-mods-menu-4-7\">7<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"8\" data-x=\"16.000\" data-y=\"80.000\" aria-label=\"8: SYSTEM READOUT\" aria-describedby=\"f-mods-menu-4-8\">8<\/button><\/div><\/div><\/div><ol class=\"mf-legend\" aria-label=\"What the numbers show\"><li data-n=\"1\" id=\"f-mods-menu-4-1\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1<\/span><div><b>INTERFACE<\/b> <span>CLASSIC or MODERN. The picture shows each one.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"2\" id=\"f-mods-menu-4-2\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2<\/span><div><b>DECK VIEW<\/b> <span>2 DECKS, 4 DECKS in number order, or 4 DECKS in mixer order.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"3\" id=\"f-mods-menu-4-3\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3<\/span><div><b>THEME<\/b> <span>The CLASSIC theme. In MODERN this place holds LAMPS AND TITLES instead.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"4\" id=\"f-mods-menu-4-4\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">4<\/span><div><b>3-BAND COLOURS<\/b> <span>A colour for the lows, mids and highs of the 3-BAND waveform. The squares show the colours in use.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"5\" id=\"f-mods-menu-4-5\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">5<\/span><div><b>WAVEFORM COLOURS<\/b> <span>STOCK, 3-BAND or STEMS. MODERN adds RGB.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"6\" id=\"f-mods-menu-4-6\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">6<\/span><div><b>KEY NOTATION<\/b> <span>AS ON THE USB, MUSICAL or WHEEL, each with an example key.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"7\" id=\"f-mods-menu-4-7\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">7<\/span><div><b>Keys and the track list<\/b> <span>PLAYING KEY, KEY MATCH COLOURS, KEY BEFORE TITLE and TRACK LIST COLUMNS.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"8\" id=\"f-mods-menu-4-8\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">8<\/span><div><b>SYSTEM READOUT<\/b> <span>CPU, memory and temperature on the top bar, on its own row at the bottom of the page.<\/span><\/div><\/li><\/ol><\/figure>\n<p><a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"screen-and-themes\">Screen, interfaces and themes<\/a> explains every item on this page. DECK VIEW is explained in <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"four-decks\" data-anchor=\"deck-view\">Four decks<\/a>.<\/p>\n<h3 id=\"m-4-decks\" data-anchor=\"4-decks\">4 DECKS<\/h3>\n<p>4 DECKS plays decks 3 and 4 over the loopback cable <span class=\"tag tag--experimental\">experimental<\/span>.<\/p>\n<figure class=\"mf\" id=\"f-mods-menu-5\"><div class=\"mf-frame\"><div class=\"mf-bar\"><span class=\"mf-label\">MODS · 4 DECKS<\/span><\/div><div class=\"mf-stage\"><img src=\"manual/shots/581f5352fbcfb967.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"MODS · 4 DECKS\" data-iface=\"modern\"><img src=\"manual/shots/63babdcc9bf912d4.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"MODS · 4 DECKS\" data-iface=\"classic\"><span class=\"mf-spot\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span><div class=\"mf-marks\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Numbered points on the picture\"><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"1\" data-x=\"42.500\" data-y=\"13.958\" aria-label=\"1: Cable state\" aria-describedby=\"f-mods-menu-5-1\">1<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"2\" data-x=\"77.500\" data-y=\"22.917\" aria-label=\"2: RESCAN\" aria-describedby=\"f-mods-menu-5-2\">2<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"3\" data-x=\"16.000\" data-y=\"37.083\" aria-label=\"3: DECK VIEW\" aria-describedby=\"f-mods-menu-5-3\">3<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"4\" data-x=\"16.000\" data-y=\"49.583\" aria-label=\"4: What works on each deck\" aria-describedby=\"f-mods-menu-5-4\">4<\/button><\/div><\/div><\/div><ol class=\"mf-legend\" aria-label=\"What the numbers show\"><li data-n=\"1\" id=\"f-mods-menu-5-1\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1<\/span><div><b>Cable state<\/b> <span>Where four decks stand, and what happens next.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"2\" id=\"f-mods-menu-5-2\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2<\/span><div><b>RESCAN<\/b> <span>Checks the cable now. Reads TRY AGAIN after a failed start.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"3\" id=\"f-mods-menu-5-3\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3<\/span><div><b>DECK VIEW<\/b> <span>How many decks the play screen shows, and in what order.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"4\" id=\"f-mods-menu-5-4\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">4<\/span><div><b>What works on each deck<\/b> <span>A tick for every deck a feature works on.<\/span><\/div><\/li><\/ol><\/figure>\n<p><a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"four-decks\">Four decks<\/a> explains the cable, every state and what decks 3 and 4 can do.<\/p>\n<h3 id=\"m-connect\" data-anchor=\"connect\">CONNECT<\/h3>\n<p>CONNECT links the player to you and to computers.<\/p>\n<figure class=\"mf\" id=\"f-mods-menu-6\"><div class=\"mf-frame\"><div class=\"mf-bar\"><span class=\"mf-label\">MODS · CONNECT<\/span><\/div><div class=\"mf-stage\"><img src=\"manual/shots/a291b11dc67a22c8.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"MODS · CONNECT\" data-iface=\"modern\"><img src=\"manual/shots/2eadaf786c662589.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"MODS · CONNECT\" data-iface=\"classic\"><span class=\"mf-spot\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span><div class=\"mf-marks\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Numbered points on the picture\"><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"1\" data-x=\"28.125\" data-y=\"22.917\" aria-label=\"1: DJ PROFILE\" aria-describedby=\"f-mods-menu-6-1\">1<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"2\" data-x=\"69.625\" data-y=\"22.917\" aria-label=\"2: VJ.TOOLS\" aria-describedby=\"f-mods-menu-6-2\">2<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"3\" data-x=\"28.125\" data-y=\"60.000\" aria-label=\"3: NETWORK\" aria-describedby=\"f-mods-menu-6-3\">3<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"4\" data-x=\"69.625\" data-y=\"60.000\" aria-label=\"4: UPDATES\" aria-describedby=\"f-mods-menu-6-4\">4<\/button><\/div><\/div><\/div><ol class=\"mf-legend\" aria-label=\"What the numbers show\"><li data-n=\"1\" id=\"f-mods-menu-6-1\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1<\/span><div><b>DJ PROFILE<\/b> <span>Your DJ name and logo from the USB, for VJ screens.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"2\" id=\"f-mods-menu-6-2\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2<\/span><div><b>VJ.TOOLS<\/b> <span>Lets VJ.Tools on a computer connect, and shows its picture instead of the play screen.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"3\" id=\"f-mods-menu-6-3\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3<\/span><div><b>NETWORK<\/b> <span>The network adapter and address, applied for this start of the player.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"4\" id=\"f-mods-menu-6-4\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">4<\/span><div><b>UPDATES<\/b> <span>Signed updates over the network. An update becomes active at the next start.<\/span><\/div><\/li><\/ol><\/figure>\n<p><a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"connect\">Connect and DJ profiles<\/a> explains every page here.<\/p>\n<h3 id=\"m-extras\" data-anchor=\"extras\">EXTRAS<\/h3>\n<figure class=\"mf\" id=\"f-mods-menu-7\"><div class=\"mf-frame\"><div class=\"mf-bar\"><span class=\"mf-label\">MODS · EXTRAS<\/span><\/div><div class=\"mf-stage\"><img src=\"manual/shots/f2c38e7b2e1d8a11.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"MODS · EXTRAS\" data-iface=\"modern\"><img src=\"manual/shots/2767bc4cad908bda.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"MODS · EXTRAS\" data-iface=\"classic\"><span class=\"mf-spot\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span><div class=\"mf-marks\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Numbered points on the picture\"><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"1\" data-x=\"28.125\" data-y=\"22.917\" aria-label=\"1: GAMES\" aria-describedby=\"f-mods-menu-7-1\">1<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"2\" data-x=\"69.625\" data-y=\"22.917\" aria-label=\"2: USB APPS\" aria-describedby=\"f-mods-menu-7-2\">2<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"3\" data-x=\"28.125\" data-y=\"60.000\" aria-label=\"3: REPORT AN ISSUE\" aria-describedby=\"f-mods-menu-7-3\">3<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"4\" data-x=\"69.625\" data-y=\"60.000\" aria-label=\"4: ABOUT XZ MODS\" aria-describedby=\"f-mods-menu-7-4\">4<\/button><\/div><\/div><\/div><ol class=\"mf-legend\" aria-label=\"What the numbers show\"><li data-n=\"1\" id=\"f-mods-menu-7-1\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1<\/span><div><b>GAMES<\/b> <span>Doom, Chex Quest, Beat Arcade, Wave Rider, Rhythm Lab and Static Surfer. The music keeps playing.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"2\" id=\"f-mods-menu-7-2\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2<\/span><div><b>USB APPS<\/b> <span>Apps for the XZ from the USB.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"3\" id=\"f-mods-menu-7-3\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3<\/span><div><b>REPORT AN ISSUE<\/b> <span>Sends a problem, a question or an idea, in three presses.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"4\" id=\"f-mods-menu-7-4\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">4<\/span><div><b>ABOUT XZ MODS<\/b> <span>Credits, links and support.<\/span><\/div><\/li><\/ol><\/figure>\n<p><a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"extras\">Extras<\/a> explains every page here.<\/p>\n<h3 id=\"m-utility-the-player-s-own-settings\" data-anchor=\"utility-the-player-s-own-settings\">UTILITY, the player's own settings<\/h3>\n<p><kbd>MENU<\/kbd> held opens the player's own UTILITY: quantize, auto cue, play mode, the display and the other stock settings.<\/p>\n<ul><li>In CLASSIC you see the player's own UTILITY screen, unchanged.<\/li><li>In MODERN, XZ Mods draws UTILITY in the MODERN look. It is the same list of stock settings, in the stock order.<\/li><li>In MODERN, MODS also has a <strong>UTILITY<\/strong> cell at the bottom of the section rail. It closes MODS and opens UTILITY. Until MODERN has read the player's settings, it reads NOT READY.<\/li><\/ul>\n<h4 id=\"m-modern-utility\" data-anchor=\"modern-utility\" data-iface=\"modern\">MODERN UTILITY <span class=\"tag tag--modern\">modern<\/span><\/h4>\n<figure class=\"mf\" id=\"f-mods-menu-8\"><div class=\"mf-frame\"><div class=\"mf-bar\"><span class=\"mf-label\">MODERN · UTILITY<\/span><\/div><div class=\"mf-stage\"><img src=\"manual/shots/b148152140a18833.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"UTILITY in MODERN, open on its first setting.\"><span class=\"mf-spot\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span><div class=\"mf-marks\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Numbered points on the picture\"><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"1\" data-x=\"5.500\" data-y=\"21.667\" aria-label=\"1: UTILITY STOCK\" aria-describedby=\"f-mods-menu-8-1\">1<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"2\" data-x=\"22.500\" data-y=\"13.750\" aria-label=\"2: Group\" aria-describedby=\"f-mods-menu-8-2\">2<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"3\" data-x=\"47.500\" data-y=\"20.625\" aria-label=\"3: Lock\" aria-describedby=\"f-mods-menu-8-3\">3<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"4\" data-x=\"78.750\" data-y=\"12.708\" aria-label=\"4: Choices\" aria-describedby=\"f-mods-menu-8-4\">4<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"5\" data-x=\"65.000\" data-y=\"37.083\" aria-label=\"5: Help\" aria-describedby=\"f-mods-menu-8-5\">5<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"6\" data-x=\"86.250\" data-y=\"3.750\" aria-label=\"6: Version\" aria-describedby=\"f-mods-menu-8-6\">6<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"7\" data-x=\"50.000\" data-y=\"89.167\" aria-label=\"7: Deck strip\" aria-describedby=\"f-mods-menu-8-7\">7<\/button><\/div><\/div><\/div><figcaption>UTILITY in MODERN, open on its first setting.<\/figcaption><ol class=\"mf-legend\" aria-label=\"What the numbers show\"><li data-n=\"1\" id=\"f-mods-menu-8-1\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1<\/span><div><b>UTILITY STOCK<\/b> <span>The player's own settings. On the player, the rail lists the MODS sections below it, and each one opens MODS on that section.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"2\" id=\"f-mods-menu-8-2\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2<\/span><div><b>Group<\/b> <span>DJ SETTING, DISPLAY (LCD), MIXER, SYSTEM and INFO, as on the player.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"3\" id=\"f-mods-menu-8-3\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3<\/span><div><b>Lock<\/b> <span>XZ Mods shows this setting but cannot change it here. The help says why.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"4\" id=\"f-mods-menu-8-4\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">4<\/span><div><b>Choices<\/b> <span>The setting's choices. The filled circle is the current one.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"5\" id=\"f-mods-menu-8-5\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">5<\/span><div><b>Help<\/b> <span>What the setting does, and what the highlighted choice means.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"6\" id=\"f-mods-menu-8-6\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">6<\/span><div><b>Version<\/b> <span>The player's firmware version.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"7\" id=\"f-mods-menu-8-7\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">7<\/span><div><b>Deck strip<\/b> <span>Decks 1 and 2 stay in view while you change settings.<\/span><\/div><\/li><\/ol><\/figure>\n<p>Turn the encoder to move through the settings and push to open the choices. Turn again to pick a choice and push to set it. <kbd>BACK<\/kbd> goes back to the list. <kbd>MENU<\/kbd> or <strong>X<\/strong> closes UTILITY.<\/p>\n<p>A lock next to a setting comes with one of these notes:<\/p>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Note<\/th><th>What it means<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>PLAYER CONTROLLED<\/td><td>The player sets this itself. XZ Mods only shows it.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>FIRMWARE LIMIT<\/td><td>XZ Mods cannot read or set it on this firmware version.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>READ-ONLY BUILD<\/td><td>A RAM trial shows settings but changes none. Start from the USB loader to change them.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>READ ONLY HERE<\/td><td>XZ Mods shows this setting but cannot change it here.<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div>\n<p>Pushing a locked setting does nothing.<\/p>\n<div class=\"mg\" id=\"f-mods-menu-9\" data-iface=\"modern\"><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/b08221cc0629ff93.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: A setting highlighted in the list\"><img src=\"manual/shots/b08221cc0629ff93.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>A setting highlighted in the list<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/7a089d8f94b145e9.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: The choices open. Turn and push to set one\"><img src=\"manual/shots/7a089d8f94b145e9.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>The choices open. Turn and push to set one<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/7a089d8f94b145e9.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: A setting XZ Mods can change, its choices open\"><img src=\"manual/shots/7a089d8f94b145e9.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>A setting XZ Mods can change, its choices open<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/3628b3123af299ea.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: A locked setting further down. Its help says it is read only here\"><img src=\"manual/shots/3628b3123af299ea.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>A locked setting further down. Its help says it is read only here<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/b83804813a3e90b8.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: The end of the list. MIXER, SYSTEM and VERSION No.\"><img src=\"manual/shots/b83804813a3e90b8.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>The end of the list. MIXER, SYSTEM and VERSION No.<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/d7608a18c6dc3e8f.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: Before the version is read. TIME MODE first, then the display settings\"><img src=\"manual/shots/d7608a18c6dc3e8f.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>Before the version is read. TIME MODE first, then the display settings<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/d7608a18c6dc3e8f.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: UTILITY on its DJ SETTING and DISPLAY (LCD) groups\"><img src=\"manual/shots/d7608a18c6dc3e8f.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>UTILITY on its DJ SETTING and DISPLAY (LCD) groups<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/fffadd4377704b9a.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: Before the decks report. The deck strip shows dashes\"><img src=\"manual/shots/fffadd4377704b9a.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>Before the decks report. The deck strip shows dashes<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/9a25dc6b33c462fc.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: SETTINGS NOT AVAILABLE HERE when the settings cannot be read\"><img src=\"manual/shots/9a25dc6b33c462fc.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>SETTINGS NOT AVAILABLE HERE when the settings cannot be read<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/4dcc1bc4e59c2b3e.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: UTILITY with four decks. A compact strip of all four decks\"><img src=\"manual/shots/4dcc1bc4e59c2b3e.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>UTILITY with four decks. A compact strip of all four decks<\/figcaption><\/figure><\/div>\n<h3 id=\"m-my-settings\" data-anchor=\"my-settings\" data-iface=\"modern\">MY SETTINGS <span class=\"tag tag--modern\">modern<\/span><\/h3>\n<p>MY SETTINGS shows the player settings saved on a USB stick, and the DJ profiles on it. In MODERN, open the stick in browse, highlight the category rail on the left, and press <kbd>MENU<\/kbd>.<\/p>\n<figure class=\"mf\" id=\"f-mods-menu-10\"><div class=\"mf-frame\"><div class=\"mf-bar\"><span class=\"mf-label\">MODERN · MY SETTINGS<\/span><\/div><div class=\"mf-stage\"><img src=\"manual/shots/0040b296fa6c4c62.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"MY SETTINGS for USB 1 while deck 1 plays.\"><span class=\"mf-spot\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span><div class=\"mf-marks\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Numbered points on the picture\"><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"1\" data-x=\"87.500\" data-y=\"12.917\" aria-label=\"1: MY SETTINGS\" aria-describedby=\"f-mods-menu-10-1\">1<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"2\" data-x=\"75.000\" data-y=\"20.833\" aria-label=\"2: Stick\" aria-describedby=\"f-mods-menu-10-2\">2<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"3\" data-x=\"95.625\" data-y=\"27.083\" aria-label=\"3: LOAD TO DECK\" aria-describedby=\"f-mods-menu-10-3\">3<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"4\" data-x=\"86.250\" data-y=\"34.167\" aria-label=\"4: SAVE TO USB 1\" aria-describedby=\"f-mods-menu-10-4\">4<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"5\" data-x=\"81.250\" data-y=\"48.333\" aria-label=\"5: DJ PROFILE\" aria-describedby=\"f-mods-menu-10-5\">5<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"6\" data-x=\"81.250\" data-y=\"62.500\" aria-label=\"6: DAMAGED\" aria-describedby=\"f-mods-menu-10-6\">6<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"7\" data-x=\"96.250\" data-y=\"69.583\" aria-label=\"7: SAVE SETTINGS TO\" aria-describedby=\"f-mods-menu-10-7\">7<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"8\" data-x=\"97.500\" data-y=\"78.125\" aria-label=\"8: Help\" aria-describedby=\"f-mods-menu-10-8\">8<\/button><\/div><\/div><\/div><figcaption>MY SETTINGS for USB 1 while deck 1 plays.<\/figcaption><ol class=\"mf-legend\" aria-label=\"What the numbers show\"><li data-n=\"1\" id=\"f-mods-menu-10-1\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1<\/span><div><b>MY SETTINGS<\/b> <span>The panel for the stick you browse. X closes it.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"2\" id=\"f-mods-menu-10-2\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2<\/span><div><b>Stick<\/b> <span>The stick whose settings these are: USB 1, USB 2, or a LINK player's USB.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"3\" id=\"f-mods-menu-10-3\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3<\/span><div><b>LOAD TO DECK<\/b> <span>Applies the settings saved on the stick to the active deck. Reads PAUSE DECK 1 TO LOAD while that deck plays.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"4\" id=\"f-mods-menu-10-4\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">4<\/span><div><b>SAVE TO USB 1<\/b> <span>Saves the player's current settings to the stick, replacing the ones there. Push once to arm it, then again to save.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"5\" id=\"f-mods-menu-10-5\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">5<\/span><div><b>DJ PROFILE<\/b> <span>The DJ profiles on the stick. Push one to make it active and apply its settings and look. ACTIVE marks the one in use.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"6\" id=\"f-mods-menu-10-6\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">6<\/span><div><b>DAMAGED<\/b> <span>A profile whose files cannot be read.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"7\" id=\"f-mods-menu-10-7\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">7<\/span><div><b>SAVE SETTINGS TO<\/b> <span>Saves the current settings into the active DJ's profile. Push twice.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"8\" id=\"f-mods-menu-10-8\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">8<\/span><div><b>Help<\/b> <span>What the highlighted row does.<\/span><\/div><\/li><\/ol><\/figure>\n<p>Further down, <strong>WAVEFORM<\/strong> sets COLOR, POSITION, ZOOM, USB COLORS and the stem row layout. <strong>SAVED ON USB 1<\/strong> lists the settings stored on the stick, which you can change there.<\/p>\n<div class=\"mg\" id=\"f-mods-menu-11\" data-iface=\"modern\"><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/ff59b4835a4f88af.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: PUSH AGAIN TO SAVE. The save is armed\"><img src=\"manual/shots/ff59b4835a4f88af.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>PUSH AGAIN TO SAVE. The save is armed<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/0ec75cb08a129a2c.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: The DJ PROFILE rows\"><img src=\"manual/shots/0ec75cb08a129a2c.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>The DJ PROFILE rows<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/2dec07fd06ffc597.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: The WAVEFORM rows\"><img src=\"manual/shots/2dec07fd06ffc597.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>The WAVEFORM rows<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/4c6eeda78d716376.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: SAVED ON USB 1. The settings on the stick, with help for the highlighted one\"><img src=\"manual/shots/4c6eeda78d716376.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>SAVED ON USB 1. The settings on the stick, with help for the highlighted one<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/98e44f460ea3d03e.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: A locked stick with nothing saved. Only the WAVEFORM rows remain\"><img src=\"manual/shots/98e44f460ea3d03e.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>A locked stick with nothing saved. Only the WAVEFORM rows remain<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/be6ae56ddb7cc8a4.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: A LINK player&#x27;s USB while deck 1 plays\"><img src=\"manual/shots/be6ae56ddb7cc8a4.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>A LINK player's USB while deck 1 plays<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/5b470cd97b1efdad.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: After a load. How many settings applied and how many do not exist on this deck\"><img src=\"manual/shots/5b470cd97b1efdad.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>After a load. How many settings applied and how many do not exist on this deck<\/figcaption><\/figure><\/div>\n<h3 id=\"m-saving-to-the-usb\" data-anchor=\"saving-to-the-usb\">Saving to the USB<\/h3>\n<p>There is no save button in MODS. Every change saves on its own to the settings USB, the stick you browse. The settings live in the VJ.Tools folder on that stick, so they travel with you to another XZ running XZ Mods. When you browse a stick, the player takes that stick's settings. A stick with no settings, or with damaged ones, leaves the current settings as they are.<\/p>\n<p>The XZ also remembers the last settings it applied. If you start it with no stick, it uses them.<\/p>\n<p>The save state at the right of the dock says what happened to your last change:<\/p>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Save state<\/th><th>What it means<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>SAVING...<\/td><td>The change is being written.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>SAVED TO USB 1 (or USB 2)<\/td><td>The change is on the stick.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>SAVED ON THIS XZ / NO USB<\/td><td>No stick is in. The change is kept on this XZ.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>SAVED ON THIS XZ / USB CHANGED<\/td><td>The settings stick changed. The change is kept on this XZ.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>SAVED ON THIS XZ / USB PROFILE KEPT<\/td><td>The stick is locked. The change is kept on this XZ and the stick is left as it was.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>USB REMOVED: SETTINGS KEPT<\/td><td>You pulled the settings stick. Nothing resets.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>NOT SAVED TO USB 1: CHECK USB<\/td><td>Writing failed. Check that the stick is in and not locked.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>NOT SAVED: USB PROFILE KEPT<\/td><td>The stick is locked and the XZ could not keep the change either.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>NO SETTINGS USB: CHANGES LAST UNTIL POWER OFF.<\/td><td>Nothing can be saved. Your change works until you switch the player off.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>NOT SAVED: CHANGES LAST UNTIL POWER OFF.<\/td><td>This build does not save settings. Changes work until you switch the player off.<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div>\n<p>Lines that say NOT SAVED or NO SETTINGS USB show in amber. DJ profiles are not settings. They stay on the DJ's stick and never on the XZ. See <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"connect\">Connect and DJ profiles<\/a>.<\/p>\n<h3 id=\"m-older-pages\" data-anchor=\"older-pages\">Older pages<\/h3>\n<p>Earlier versions had GENERAL, CONTROLS, THEMES and SETTINGS pages in MODS. They are gone. Anything that pointed at them now opens the page that replaced them:<\/p>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Old page<\/th><th>Opens<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>GENERAL<\/td><td>HOME<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>CONTROLS<\/td><td>STEM PADS, in STEMS<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>THEMES<\/td><td>SCREEN<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>SETTINGS<\/td><td>PLAY<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div>";
